

The process of telecom churn analysis starts with cleaning and understanding the data, followed by exploring customer demographics, services, billing, and contract details to identify churn patterns. 
After preparing the data with encoding and scaling, machine learning models such as Logistic Regression or Random Forest are trained to predict which customers are likely to leave.
The results are evaluated using metrics like ROC-AUC and Precision-Recall, and feature importance is analyzed to understand key churn drivers.
Finally, customers are segmented into risk groups, and actionable strategies—such as offering discounts to month-to-month users or improving onboarding for new customers—are recommended to reduce churn.
